  "catalogPath": "grapher/biodiversity/2026-05-29/long_run_whaling/long_run_whaling_annual#fin",
  "descriptionShort": "Number of Fin Whales caught annually",
  "descriptionFromProducer": "- The year is the \"defined catch year,\" usually the year in which all catches were taken. For Antarctic operations it is defined as the start of the season (e.g. for the 1985/86 Antarctic Season the year is 1985).\n- The country is the country of the operating company.\n- All numbers include lost whales (whales that were injured or killed but then lost at sea).",
  "descriptionProcessing": "- Data after 1985 comes from the International Whaling Commission (IWC) which recorded the number of catches at: https://iwc.int/management-and-conservation/whaling/total-catches\n- Data pre-1985 comes from: Rocha, R. C., Clapham, P. J., & Ivashchenko, Y. V. (2014). Emptying the oceans: a summary of industrial whaling catches in the 20th century. Marine Fisheries Review, 76(4), 37-48.\n- For continuity with the Rocha data, we combine common minke and Antarctic minke into a single 'minke' category, and blue and pygmy blue whales into a single 'blue' category. We also add bowhead whales to the \"other/unspecified\" category in the Rocha data, as they are included in the IWC data but not in Rocha's.",
  "type": "int",
  "dataChecksum": "1997423022456094364",
